@module arrangeView  src=arrangeView.lua  loc=1012  mode=chunk  self=av
@deps cm, cmgr, facade, am

# Invariants & contracts
  @invariant  av owns arrange-page state — cursor, scroll, selection, paletteSlot; page renders.  @ 4
  @invariant  page builds am and injects it; av owns the ref — all mutations route through av.  @ 5
  @invariant  av speaks no ImGui — modifiers arrive as plain booleans; av works in QN/rows only.  @ 6
  @invariant  cursor/scroll are in-memory module-locals; only beatPerRow persists via cm.  @ 7
  @invariant  cursorRow is integer rows; cursorCol is 0-based track index. qn = row * beatPerRow.  @ 8
  @invariant  gridRows/gridCols set by the page each frame; followViewport runs on every cursor move.  @ 9
  @invariant  av registers arrange-scope command bodies; page owns key bindings and createSlot.  @ 10
  @invariant  selection is a per-session set of take handles; setFocus/focus are single-element.  @ 11
  @invariant  a Shift+arrow band lasts until the first command that isn't a Shift+arrow.  @ 12
  @invariant  replace mode lasts until the drop it reinterprets, or the first other command.  @ 13
  @invariant  paletteSlot is per-session (0..61 or nil) — palette's highlighted row; not cursorCol.  @ 14
  @invariant  edit cmds target via actionTargets; off-screen + nothing selected = no-op.  @ 242
  @invariant  drop0..dropZ place a fresh instance at the cursor and advance the caret past it.  @ 393
  @invariant  arrangeAdvanceBy0..9 (Ctrl+digit) set the step; arrangeAdvanceMode (Ctrl-`) picks it.  @ 394
  @invariant  drop on an empty slot is a no-op; new takes arrive at the slot's full pool length.  @ 395
  @invariant  drop over a take starting at the cursor overwrites it; drops never stack.  @ 396
  @invariant  a drop while armed stands the slot in for every action target.  @ 466
  @invariant  each replacement keeps its target's start; each arrives at its own natural length.  @ 467
  @invariant  a held selection passes to the replacements; a cursor-driven replace selects nothing.  @ 468
  @invariant  a lone replacement pulls the cursor in. The drop disarms either way.  @ 469
  @contract  returns { ghosts={{take,startQN,lengthQN,headQN},…}, fits }; one ghost per member.  @ 799
  @contract  headQN is the source a ghost would elide above its start; a move carries its own along.  @ 800
  @contract  fits false iff any ghost's destination start is occupied.  @ 801
  @contract  move/dup ghost = naturalLenQN; a tail resize grows/shrinks from the current rendered  @ 802
  @contract  length, a head resize from the held end back to the origin.  @ 803

